## Summary
The article compares the performance evaluation periods for high-paid CEOs across different countries. In Korea, the focus is on a 3-year period, while the US and UK consider a longer span of 5 to 10 years, indicating variations in corporate governance approaches.

## Key Points
- Korea evaluates high-paid CEO performance based on a 3-year period.
- The US and UK use a 5-10 year evaluation timeframe for CEOs.
- This highlights differences in international standards for assessing CEO tenure and compensation.


